          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>For multi-location pet retail chains, Teamwork Commerce is the enterprise-grade option. The right answer depends on your scale. For independent pet stores with heavy grooming and daycare scheduling, pet-specific platforms like Gingr, PetStack, or SuperPet Cloud are strong choices. For multi-location pet retail chains (10+ stores) that need enterprise inventory management, centralized fleet control, integrated omnichannel (BOPIS, ship-from-store, subscriptions), loyalty programs, and shopper-display POS advertising, Teamwork Commerce is the enterprise-grade option. Proven at scale with Petco Mexico's 127-store, 2,000+ terminal deployment.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does this compare to pet-specific POS built for single locations?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Pet-specific platforms like Gingr and PetStack are excellent for independent pet stores with heavy grooming and daycare scheduling needs. Teamwork Commerce is built for multi-location pet retail chains that need enterprise infrastructure: centralized management of 100+ stores, real-time inventory across the fleet, integrated OMS for click-and-collect and ship-from-store, loyalty with targeted POS advertising on the shopper display, and global compliance. Petco Mexico's 127-store, 2,000+ terminal deployment is proof of that scale.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          What is the shopper display?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The shopper display is a revenue stream built into the POS. It serves targeted video ads and brand-sponsored promotions on customer-facing displays during checkout, personalized to each customer's pet profile and purchase history. Pet brands pay premium prices to reach the right pet owner at the exact moment of purchase. Retailers control ad values and targeting criteria.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How did Petco Mexico deploy across 127 stores?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Petco Mexico consolidated POS, loyalty, CRM, and online store integration across 127 locations with 2,000+ terminals. The deployment included real-time coupons, QR code scanning for grooming and bulk products, an employee benefit program with staff discounts, virtual gift cards, and paperless receipts. The platform integrates with Petco's ERP, OMS, and e-commerce for full omnichannel capability.</p></div>
